    answer: 0,
    explanation: {"en":"In SSDs, data cannot be directly overwritten; a memory block must first be erased before new data is written. Garbage collection removes invalid or unused data blocks to free space for future writes. SSDs support random access and can store large files, and garbage collection is mainly related to write management, not read latency.","bn":"In SSDs, data cannot be directly overwritten; a memory block must first be erased before new data is written. Garbage collection removes invalid or unused data blocks to free space for future writes. SSDs support random access and can store large files, and garbage collection is mainly related to write management, not read latency."},
