    topic: "daa",
    question: {"en":"What is the worst case time complexity of inserting n elements into an empty linked list, if the linked list needs to be maintained in sorted order?","bn":"What is the worst case time complexity of inserting n elements into an empty linked list, if the linked list needs to be maintained in sorted order?"},
    options: [{"en":"Θ(n)","bn":"Θ(n)"}, {"en":"Θ(n log n)","bn":"Θ(n log n)"}, {"en":"Θ(n²)","bn":"Θ(n²)"}, {"en":"Θ(1)","bn":"Θ(1)"}],
    answer: 2,
    explanation: {"en":"If we insert elements one by one into a sorted linked list: 1st element → O(1) 2nd element → compare with 1 element → O(1) 3rd element → compare with 2 elements → O(2) … nth element → compare with (n−1) elements → O(n−1) Total comparisons: 1 + 2 + 3 + ... + (n−1) = n(n−1)/2 = Θ(n²) So, worst-case time complexity is Θ(n²).","bn":"If we insert elements one by one into a sorted linked list: 1st element → O(1) 2nd element → compare with 1 element → O(1) 3rd element → compare with 2 elements → O(2) … nth element → compare with (n−1) elements → O(n−1) Total comparisons: 1 + 2 + 3 + ... + (n−1) = n(n−1)/2 = Θ(n²) So, worst-case time complexity is Θ(n²)."},
    difficulty: "medium",
    source: "Bangladesh Bank Assistant Director (ICT) · 2025",
