    question: {"en":"A system has 6 identical resources and N processes competing for them. Each process can request at most 2 resources. Which one of the following values of N could lead to a deadlock?","bn":"A system has 6 identical resources and N processes competing for them. Each process can request at most 2 resources. Which one of the following values of N could lead to a deadlock?"},
    options: [{"en":"1","bn":"1"}, {"en":"2","bn":"2"}, {"en":"3","bn":"3"}, {"en":"4","bn":"4"}],
    answer: 3,
    explanation: {"en":"Deadlock can occur if every process holds one resource and waits for another. With 4 processes, each could hold 1 resource (total used = 4) and wait for one more. If the remaining resources are not sufficient to satisfy any waiting request pattern, a circular wait may occur. Thus, N = 4 can lead to a deadlock scenario.","bn":"Deadlock can occur if every process holds one resource and waits for another. With 4 processes, each could hold 1 resource (total used = 4) and wait for one more. If the remaining resources are not sufficient to satisfy any waiting request pattern, a circular wait may occur. Thus, N = 4 can lead to a deadlock scenario."},
